# Redis local setup

Run Redis in Docker:

```bash
docker run --name local-redis -p 6379:6379 -d redis:7
```

Open the Redis CLI:

```bash
docker exec -it local-redis redis-cli
```

Test it:

```redis
PING
SET message "Hello, Redis!"
GET message
```

Python example (install with `python -m pip install redis`):

```python
import redis

client = redis.Redis(host="localhost", port=6379, decode_responses=True)
client.set("message", "Hello, Redis!")
print(client.get("message"))
```
